    "result_text": "All changes are in place and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `householdId` is now a deterministic, self-computing value rather than a link created on demand.\n\n**`HouseholdResolver.deriveHouseholdId`** \u2014 now keys on `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`. It returns the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` (normalized = trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased). Dropped the now-unused `AddressNormalizer` dependency and the old `HH-` prefix, matching the spec's exact wording.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1`:**\n- `assignHouseholdId(owner)` \u2014 every owner with a postcode gets the deterministic id automatically (owners with no postcode keep `null`, so they never match as a household). Removed `findHouseholdMembers`, `computeHouseholdId`, and `backfillHouseholdMembers` \u2014 deterministic derivation makes matching/backfilling unnecessary.\n- New `requireHouseholdNotDuplicate(owner, dto)` \u2014 if an existing owner already carries the same `householdId`, the create is rejected with **409** unless the payload sets `sharesHousehold`, which declares the owner a genuine household member and lets it through.\n- `flagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is never flagged as a possible duplicate.\n- `requireUniqueIdentity` still folds the (now deterministic) `householdId` into the identity key, and `populateHouseholdMemberCount` (the household-size input) already counts by `householdId`, so both now key off the computed value.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions to match the new behavior.\n\nThe scenario from the acceptance test now holds: two owners with the same last name + postcode share an identical `householdId` (the second needs `sharesHousehold` to bypass the 409), while a different last name yields a different id.\n\n`mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
